<title>FRANCE: New York top gateway for French imports.</title>
<headline>New York top gateway for French imports.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Paris airports authority, the Aeroports de Paris (ADP), said New York was the top originating gateway for import traffic into Charles de Gaulle and Orly airports last month despite a steep decline in tonnage.</p>
<p>October 1996 New York-Paris air cargo volume totalled 3,070 tonnes, down 22.9 percent on the same month last year, ADP figures showed.</p>
<p>Chicago was in second place with 2,390 tonnes, little changed on October 1995.</p>
<p>Hong Kong was ranked third with 2,201 tonnes flown into Paris, a rise of 8.2 percent on 1995 levels, ADP said.</p>
<p>The top ten airport gateways for ADP imports in October 1996 and the percentage change on October 1995 were:</p>
<p>  1  New York	 3,070 tonnes  down 22.9pct</p>
<p>  2  Chicago	  2,390 tonnes	  0.0</p>
<p>  3  Hong Kong	2,201 tonnes  up    8.2</p>
<p>  4  Tokyo	    1,776 tonnes  up    7.1</p>
<p>  5  Los Angeles    1,301 tonnes  down  9.5</p>
<p>  6  Montreal	 1,015 tonnes  down  4.4</p>
<p>  7  Miami		694 tonnes  down  2.8</p>
<p>  8  Johannesburg     516 tonnes  up   10.2</p>
<p>  9  Singapore	  499 tonnes  down 22.1</p>
<p>  10 Casablanca	 394 tonnes  down  8.0</p>
